🚽 Test case: #193 -- passing a struct POINTER variable where a by-value
🚽 struct argument is expected (`show(pp)` with `gang Point *pp`) is a type
🚽 error, not an implicit dereference. The identifier arm enforces the same
🚽 pointer_level == 0 invariant as the member-access arm (PR #253 review,
🚽 finding 1).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};

skibidi show(gang Point p) {
    yapping("%d", p.x);
}

skibidi main {
    gang Point q;
    q.x = 5;
    gang Point *pp = &q;
    show(pp);
}
